  "body": "https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/parsing.html#parsing-main-inbody\r\n\r\n> A character token that is U\\+0000 NULL\r\n> \r\n>     Parse error. Ignore the token.\r\n\r\nA parse error is already reported in the tokenization stage (for example in [the data state](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/parsing.html#data-state), so it seems odd that a second one would be reported immediately after. Is it safe to assume these are editorial relics?",
